SUMMARY:Fall Trail Day
DESCRIPTION:Fall Trail Day\nOctober 17\, 2026\nHike\, bike or run to join us for Trail Day at the Arboretum! Join us October 17 as we celebrate all things trails! Nearly all our 10 miles of hiking and biking trails are reopened\, so you can also choose your own adventure. Grab a drink from the Garden Shed or refuel at the water station located in the Rec Lot.  \nSchedule\nTrails and Ales Guided Walk\n10:30 & 12:30\n\n\nEnjoy a fall guided hike and afterwards a cold Highland brew at the Garden Shed! \n\n\n\n\nJoin an experienced guide for a beautiful fall walk through the Arboretum’s scenic trails! Along the way\, discover the native plants and learn about the rich history of the surrounding landscape. After your adventure\, unwind with a crisp beer from Highland Brewing at the Garden Shed on Baker Lawn. Each participant will receive one beverage voucher\, redeemable for an alcoholic or non-alcoholic beverage exclusively at the Garden Shed. \nCheers to Highland Brewing for sponsoring this autumn adventure! Parking fee not included. \nRegister Here for the Trails and Ales Walk\nFree Guided Walk\n11:00 – leaves from Baker Visitor Center\nTrail First Aid Demo – Presented by Landmark Learning\n12:00 & 2:00 – Baker Visiter Center
URL:https://ncarboretum.org/event/fall-trail-day-2/
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ncarboretum.org/wp-content/uploads/2023/10/20231017_cantrell_fallgarden_021-scaled.jpg
END:VEVENT
